// Hakuro's arms as his sampled grids had them, kept when the grids went (rywible/wrela#430 is
// the last revision that holds them): each arm's radius about its chain at rest (m), read along
// rays from the chain's path as the forms tool reads a reference (`targets::every_ray`), on a
// grid of `ALONG` places along `SPAN` of the path by `ROUND` round it, each half a step on from
// the grid's own. His arms' forms were fitted to the same grids at four times as many places;
// these are what the forms are measured against now (`tests`), so a change to the figure's arm,
// its chain or the form's basis that moved his arm would show.

use engine::chart::Sample
use std::math::TAU

/// How many places the radii were read at along the span, and round the path.
pub const ALONG: u32 = 32
pub const ROUND: u32 = 13

/// The span of each arm's path the radii cover: from where it leaves his jacket to inside the
/// wrap or the gauntlet at his wrist.
pub const SPAN: vec2 = vec2(0.14, 0.84)

